      "id": "at-glance",
      "title": "At a glance",
      "body": "For travelers, Tôi có đặt phòng is the phrase to keep ready for \"I have a reservation\" in front desk, room, check-in, and hotel-service moments. This is for the desk when you have already booked. At check-in, reservation first is usually the fastest path. It works best when you focus on putting the booking first so staff can look it up before you explain more. After you say it, listen for a name check, booking-code request, counter direction, or short wait; the next rows help you keep the exchange moving.",
      "presentation": "plain-text"
    },
